uded from pooled RR CIs including 1; CI method not stated\",\"role\":\"ancillary\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"The frequency of SAEs across both trials was similar in the intervention (4.3%) and control (4.1%) groups\"},{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"(pooled RR = 1.02; 95% CI = 0.91–1.15)\"}]}],\"comparison\":{\"framework\":\"pair\",\"scale\":\"relative\",\"referent\":\"placebo recipients\",\"across\":[\"vaccine vs placebo receipt\"],\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"occurred in 3.8% of the intervention group participants, compared with 0.9% of the control group participants\"}]},\"inference\":{\"v\":\"CIs and tests\",\"method_stated\":false,\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"(pooled RR = 1.02; 95% CI = 0.91–1.15)\"}]},\"primary_measures\":[{\"v\":\"pooled relative risk\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"table 2\",\"q\":\"Pooled relative risk for events in all included trials for each outcome.\"}]},{\"v\":\"percentage\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"table 2\",\"q\":\"RSVPreF3 recipients no./No. (%)\"}]}],\"regression_fields\":null,\"public_health_question\":{\"v\":\"What evidence on efficacy and safety supports ACIP's recommendation of RSV vaccines for adults aged ≥60 years, and how should they be used?\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"to review available evidence regarding the safety, immunogenicity, and efficacy of these vaccines among adults aged ≥60 years\"}]},\"conditions\":[{\"v\":\"respiratory syncytial virus (RSV) lower respiratory tract disease\",\"role\":\"vaccine target\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"title\",\"q\":\"Use of Respiratory Syncytial Virus Vaccines in Older Adults\"}]},{\"v\":\"serious adverse events\",\"role\":\"outcome\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"The frequency of serious adverse events (SAEs)*** across both trials\"}]},{\"v\":\"severe reactogenicity\",\"role\":\"outcome\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"table 2\",\"q\":\"Severe reactogenicity events\"}]},{\"v\":\"inflammatory neurologic events (Guillain-Barré syndrome, ADEM)\",\"role\":\"outcome\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"inflammatory neurologic events were reported in three of 17,922 participants within 42 days after receipt of the GSK vaccine\"}]},{\"v\":\"atrial fibrillation\",\"role\":\"outcome\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"reported atrial fibrillation as an unsolicited event within the 30 days after injection\"}]}],\"study_design\":[{\"v\":\"guidance or recommendations\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"summary\",\"q\":\"the Advisory Committee on Immunization Practices recommended that persons aged ≥60 years may receive a single dose of RSV vaccine, using shared clinical decision-making\"}]},{\"v\":\"review or synthesis\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"A systematic review of published and unpublished evidence of the efficacy and safety of these vaccines among persons aged ≥60 years was conducted.\"}]}],\"data_source_type\":[{\"v\":\"other\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"one phase 3 randomized controlled trial and one combined phase 1 and 2 (phase 1/2) randomized controlled trial for each vaccine\"},{\"loc\":\"table 2\",\"q\":\"Additional data provided by GSK.\"}]}],\"data_source_named\":[{\"v\":\"GSK RSVPreF3 phase 3 and phase 1/2 trials\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"table 2\",\"q\":\"observed in GSK’s pivotal phase 3 trial\"}]},{\"v\":\"Pfizer RSVpreF phase 3 and phase 1/2 trials\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"table 4\",\"q\":\"Safety events observed in Pfizer’s pivotal phase 3 trial\"}]}],\"setting\":{\"v\":\"international\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"phase 3 clinical trial conducted in 17 countries and including 24,973 immunocompetent participants aged ≥60 years\"}]},\"vaccine_outcome_type\":{\"v\":\"effectiveness\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"summary\",\"q\":\"vaccination with a single RSV vaccine dose demonstrated moderate to high efficacy in preventing symptomatic RSV-associated LRTD among adults aged ≥60 years\"}]},\"equity\":{\"level\":0,\"level_reason\":\"Age (≥60 years) only defines the population; frailty and long-term care residence are clinical or setting risk factors, not social position. Equity appears only as an Evidence to Recommendation domain.\",\"level_confidence\":\"high\",\"level_alternative\":{\"level\":1,\"reason\":\"Equity is named as a domain the Work Group reviewed, which could be read as raising equity without analysis.\"},\"dimensions\":[{\"v\":\"age\",\"role\":\"population\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"title\",\"q\":\"Use of Respiratory Syncytial Virus Vaccines in Older Adults\"}]}],\"determinants_of_health\":{\"v\":null,\"ev\":[]},\"equity_action\":{\"v\":false,\"ev\":[]},\"equity_measurement\":null},\"groupwise\":[],\"uncertain_fields\":[\"data_focus\",\"procedures\"],\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"notes\":\"Efficacy estimates (and their age/region adjustment and multiplicity-adjusted CIs) are manufacturer-calculated and cited, so they are not recorded as the article's own procedures or outcomes. The pooled safety RRs across trials appear to be the Work Group's own computation, which is why data_focus is yes rather than limited. GRADE certainty ratings are in external tables.\",\"view_issues\":\"Footnote † says report VE estimates differ from CDC's GRADE-table estimates because a different method was used; the pooled RR method is not stated.\"}", "type": "text"}]}